<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pope Boniface VIII</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1230–1303</span> · Also known as Benedetto Caetani</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pope Boniface VIII, born Benedetto Caetani, was pope from 1294 to 1303. He proclaimed the first Jubilee in 1300, issued the bull Unam sanctam in 1302 asserting papal supremacy, and in 1297 granted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corsica">Corsica</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-ii-of-aragon">James II of Aragon</a>. His conflict with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-iv-of-france">Philip IV of France</a> ended in his seizure at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anagni">Anagni</a> in 1303, shortly before his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-boniface-viii.jpg" alt="Pope Boniface VIII" width="320" height="440" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giotto · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Giotto_-_Bonifatius_VIII_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
